   "text": "full volume",
   "originalText": "full volume",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1128,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100070,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700490,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Send 10 million messages from a fresh IP on day one and most will be rejected or spam-foldered - and the resulting complaint\nand bounce rates DAMAGE THE IP'S REPUTATION, making the problem self-reinforcing. So volume is ramped gradually, letting each\nprovider observe good behaviour at each level. Roughly 2 to 6 weeks per IP, and Gmail, Outlook and Yahoo each maintain\nindependent reputation and must each observe the ramp separately.",
   "originalText": "Send 10 million messages from a fresh IP on day one and most will be rejected or spam-foldered - and the resulting complaint\nand bounce rates DAMAGE THE IP'S REPUTATION, making the problem self-reinforcing. So volume is ramped gradually, letting each\nprovider observe good behaviour at each level. Roughly 2 to 6 weeks per IP, and Gmail, Outlook and Yahoo each maintain\nindependent reputation and must each observe the ramp separately.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1180,
   "y": 938,
   "width": 442,
   "height": 165,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100071,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700497,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Three architectural consequences:\n\nnew sending capacity has WEEKS of lead time - you cannot\nadd outbound throughput in response to demand\n\nlosing an IP is EXPENSIVE - a blocklisted IP takes weeks to\nreplace, so protecting reputation is protecting capacity\n\nthe IP pool is a MANAGED RESOURCE with per-IP, per-provider\nvolume budgets - which is why the reputation / IP pool\nmanager is a first-class component and not a config file",
   "originalText": "Three architectural consequences:\n\nnew sending capacity has WEEKS of lead time - you cannot\nadd outbound throughput in response to demand\n\nlosing an IP is EXPENSIVE - a blocklisted IP takes weeks to\nreplace, so protecting reputation is protecting capacity\n\nthe IP pool is a MANAGED RESOURCE with per-IP, per-provider\nvolume budgets - which is why the reputation / IP pool\nmanager is a first-class component and not a config file",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
